Some general remarks: 

- You should have everything fixed and done _before_ waking 
  up Rodney in hell.  Don't drag pets with you who could 
  wake him by theirselves.  

- Rodney keeps coming back, and also curses your inventory.   
  The conclusion is to make as much haste as possible; have 
  a clear direct path from each level entrance to exit. 

- With the amulet, using spells consumes more food.  So, if 
  you want to port to the upstairs, use a wand if you have a 
  surplus.  

- Rodney wants to steal the amulet, besides other things.  
  Be careful while fighting him; if he gets away he may have 
  taken the amulet with him.  Check your inventory regularly.  

- He likes summoning nasties, which can be a very bad thing 
  (I once had two master mind flayers summoned by him, which 
  is great if you are on the fast race towards lvl 1 :-/).  
  The faster you kill him, the better.  A cockatrice corpse 
  is wonderful.  

- On the planes, you shouldn't waste time; locate the portal 
  and run for it.  (Read spoilers for how to determine the 
  portal.)

- On air, conflict can buy you some time off the really 
  nasty air elementals.  Use !o full healing generously.  

- On water, be careful not to stand adjacent to water.  

- If your gloves get cursed, you can't switch rings, so be 
  sure to have them uncursed.  

- On astral plane, death-zap famine and pestilence and try to 
  avoid death.  Try to take out priests fast and blind yourself 
  when fighting archons.  

- One of the most nasty twitches are NPCs on astral plane.  
  The most dangerous one I ever met was using a bullwhip to 
  *disarm* me.  This is extremely dangerous because you 
  are not used to it and by chance will not even recognize.  
  Carry a back-up weapon with you.  

